  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nAfter some early morning low clouds and fog, confidence is high\nthat fair weather will prevail today through at least \nWednesday. Broad high pressure over southern Canada will be the \nsource of this fair weather as it drifts east through the week. \nAs the high remains centered north of the area, temperatures \nwill trend cooler than normal for both day time highs and \novernight lows. This will translate to highs in the low to mid \n60s and lows in the 30s to 40s. There will likely be favorable \nradiational cooling conditions most nights and it is likely some\nspots south of the mountains will see some frost.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\n\nAt the end of the week, models have consistently shown the \npotential for a coastal low to impact the region. A high degree \nof storm track uncertainty still remains, but the low could \nallow for some much needed rainfall over the weekend if the low \ntakes a more westerly or northerly track. Gusty winds and high \nsurf could be possible as well.",
